From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 05:10:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/17] fix(runtime): VIF1 keeps DIRECT commands when a GIF
 image spans them

When a PATH2 IMAGE packet was longer than its DIRECT, the interpreter
swallowed whatever followed as image data. Games send the rest as the
payload of the next DIRECT/DIRECTHL, behind its own VIFcode: SLES-55605
does NOP + DIRECTHL 0x4000. The VIFcode was eaten, the stream slipped by
8 bytes, texture data was parsed as commands, and a bogus MSCAL ran an
empty VU1 program.

The rest of an image is now fed from following DIRECT payloads; raw
qwords with no DIRECT in front still continue the image as before. A
DIRECT cut off by the end of a transfer is tracked on its own and
resumes at the start of the next one.

Co-Authored-By: Lisvindanu <lisvindanu015@gmail.com>
